ly with moves like d6, Nc6, and Nf6, creating pressure\n- The Bird\'s Opening is somewhat risky for White, and e5 punishes the weakening of White\'s kingside\n- It leads to sharp, tactical play where Black gets good piece activity\n- This is the most principled and theoretically sound response to f2-f4\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e5'}
