 strongest move. It gives check to the White king, forcing an immediate response, and simultaneously attacks the rook on h1. After White moves the king (likely Ke1-e2, Ke1-f1, or Ke1-d2), I can capture the rook on h1 with Nf2xh1, winning significant material (a rook is worth about 5 pawns). This tactical blow gives me a decisive material advantage.\n\nAnswer: N: g4-f2"}
