ical crisis for White. Even if White captures it next turn, I'll have forced their pieces into awkward positions. If White cannot deal with it immediately (which seems difficult given their king is on b4 and pieces are poorly coordinated), I'll promote to a queen and gain overwhelming material advantage. This is the most forcing, concrete continuation that maximizes winning chances.\n\nAnswer: P: e3-e2"}
