l key central squares (d4, e5)\n- It prepares further development while maintaining flexibility\n- Given White's exposed king on a2, I want to develop my pieces quickly to potentially launch an attack\n- This move follows sound opening principles: develop knights before bishops, control the center\n\nAnswer: N: b8-c6"}
