son: The White king on a2 is extremely vulnerable with limited escape squares. By playing N: c6-b4, I attack the king directly while also controlling c2 and d3. The king will be forced to move (likely to a1, a3, or b3), and I can continue applying pressure. This aggressive move capitalizes on White's king safety issues and gives me the best practical winning chances.\n\nAnswer: N: c6-b4"}
