 an immediate response. After the king moves (likely Ka1-b1 is the only legal move since a2 is controlled by the knight), I'll have gained time and improved my knight's position. The check is forcing and maintains the initiative, which is critical in chess. The White king's exposed position is a major weakness I should exploit immediately.\n\nAnswer: N: b4-c2"}
