ltiple objectives: it centralizes the knight on an excellent square, controls critical central territory, supports potential pawn breaks (like f7-f5 or d7-d5), and maintains maximum flexibility for future operations. The d4 square is a classic strong outpost for a knight, and from there it can quickly redeploy to attack or defense as needed. This move maintains my initiative while improving my position.\n\nAnswer: N: c2-d4"}
