ive position and limits their options. The knight on d2 would be excellently placed, controlling key squares and maintaining pressure. When you have the opportunity to check an exposed king, especially one that has moved away from its defenses, it's almost always the right choice as it seizes the initiative.\n\nAnswer: N: b3-d2"}
