lently placed on b3, controlling important squares and potentially winning material or creating further threats.\n\nReason: N: d2-b3 gives check, forcing White's hand and maintaining my active knight in White's position. This move seizes the initiative and puts immediate pressure on White's exposed king, which is a critical advantage in this position.\n\nAnswer: N: d2-b3"}
