g key central squares and putting pressure on White's cramped position. Given White's exposed king on a2, creating tactical complications and maintaining piece activity is crucial. The fork threat on the rook is immediate and forcing, giving me tempo to improve my position further.\n\nAnswer: N: b3-d2"}
