 path to victory.\n\nReason: N: d2-f3 is the strongest move because it attacks both the White rook on h2 and the g3 pawn simultaneously (a fork). The rook will be forced to move, and I can then capture the g3 pawn or continue pressuring White's position. This concrete tactical blow leverages my material advantage and puts immediate pressure on White's position.\n\nAnswer: N: d2-f3"}
