ce and perfectly positioned to create threats. **N: b2-d3** is the strongest move because:\n- It centralizes the knight on an excellent outpost\n- Controls key squares (b4, c5, e5, f4, etc.)\n- Puts pressure on White's position\n- Keeps the knight safe while maintaining maximum activity\n- Supports potential pawn breaks with d7-d5 or c7-c5 in the future\n\nAnswer: N: b2-d3"}
