 rank with limited squares, this creates immediate tactical pressure. After Re1, White's rook must move (likely Rg2 or similar), and I maintain a powerful, active rook position while potentially controlling the first rank. This is much more concrete than giving a check with Re5, which just pushes the king without achieving a tangible advantage.\n\nAnswer: R: e4-e1"}
