g\n- After the king moves, I can continue to harass it or improve my position\n\nReason: Giving check with the rook is a fundamental principle - when you can give check safely and force your opponent's king into a worse position, you should strongly consider it. White's king on d3 is already dangerously centralized and exposed. By checking from d1, I force the king to move while maintaining my rook's activity on a dominant file/rank. This keeps maximum pressure and initiative.\n\nAnswer: R: c1-d1"}
