eck to the White king on f4 (the rook would attack from f3). This forcing move gains tempo, improves my rook's activity, and puts immediate pressure on White's exposed king. After the king moves, I can continue to use my active rook to dominate the position and support my pawns. Checks should always be carefully considered as they limit the opponent's options.\n\nAnswer: R: d3-f3"}
