re (likely Kf4, Kf6, or Kg4). This maintains the initiative and keeps my Rook actively placed. With my material advantage (extra Rook and Bishop), I should press the attack rather than play passively. After the King moves, I can continue to dominate with my Rook and potentially coordinate with my other pieces for a winning attack.\n\nAnswer: R: e1-e5"}
