opens the diagonal for my bishop (c8 can go to d7, e6, or f5 later)\n- It opens the c-file for my rook\n- It challenges White's central control\n- It creates potential counterplay against White's advanced king\n- It breaks the static pawn structure that's strangling my position\n\nThis move is essential to activate my pieces before White's positional advantage becomes overwhelming.\n\n**Answer:** P: c7-c5"}
