e:\n- It gives check to the White king on f2\n- Forces the king to move to a worse square (likely f3, f1, or g1)\n- After the king moves, I can potentially capture the g3 pawn or continue applying pressure\n- It maximizes my active piece advantage and puts White on the defensive\n- With my material advantage, forcing play and attacking is the clearest path to victory\n\nAnswer: R: e8-e2"}
