ngs the king into play, allowing it to support the pawns (particularly c5 and f7) and contest White's central control. With an active king, Black can coordinate with the bishop to create threats. Delaying king activation would allow White to consolidate the advantage in king position.\n\n**Answer:** K: g8-f8"}
