 the strongest move because:\n- It directly attacks White's knight on g1, forcing it to move\n- It centralizes my bishop on an excellent square\n- It maintains flexibility for my king and pawns\n- It creates immediate tactical pressure rather than slow positional improvements\n- The knight will have to retreat, giving me tempo to improve my position\n\nAnswer: B: f1-d3"}
