ely blockade it with my bishop by playing B: a8-b7. This prevents the pawn from advancing while keeping my bishop active. From b7, the bishop controls important central squares and maintains the blockade. Any other move allows White to push a7-a8 and promote, which would likely be losing for me.\n\nAnswer: B: a8-b7"}
